 # 36\. Accounting Integrity Validation

 Before delivering the workbook, programmatically validate all of the following:

 ### General Ledger

 - Debits = Credits
- GL agrees with journal entries
- Account balances calculate correctly

 ### AP

 - AP subledger = AP control account
- Invoice totals are correct
- Payment totals are correct
- Aging is correct

 ### AR

 - AR subledger = AR control account
- Invoice totals are correct
- Receipt totals are correct
- Aging is correct

 ### Bank

 - Opening balance + transactions = ending balance
- Reconciliation can be performed

 ### Inventory

 - Beginning quantity + purchases − sales ± adjustments = ending quantity
- Inventory value is mathematically correct

 ### Fixed Assets

 - Cost − accumulated depreciation = net book value

 ### GST

 - Transaction-level GST = reporting-period GST
- GST control account reconciles

 ### Payroll

 - Payroll entries balance and post correctly

 ### Trial Balance

 - Debits = Credits

 ### Financial Statements

 - P&L agrees with GL
- Balance Sheet agrees with GL
- Net income flows correctly into equity
- Cash Flow reconciles to cash movement

 ### Referential Integrity

 All required foreign keys must point to valid records.

